{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Viewport\/anisotropicFilteringLevel","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"title":"anisotropicFilteringLevel","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"anisotropicFilteringLevel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Viewport","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot8ViewportC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot8ViewportC20AnisotropicFilteringO","text":"AnisotropicFiltering"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot8ViewportC25anisotropicFilteringLevelAC011AnisotropicE0Ovp","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets the maximum number of samples to take when using anisotropic filtering on textures (as a power of two). A higher sample count will result in sharper textures at oblique angles, but is more expensive to compute. A value of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" forcibly disables anisotropic filtering, even on materials where it is enabled."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Viewport"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"anisotropicFilteringLevel","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Viewport","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot8ViewportC","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Viewport"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Viewport\/AnisotropicFiltering","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot8ViewportC20AnisotropicFilteringO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AnisotropicFiltering"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The anisotropic filtering level also affects decals and light projectors if they are configured to use anisotropic filtering. See ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/textures\/decals\/filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ProjectSettings\/rendering\/textures\/lightProjectors\/filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In 3D, for this setting to have an effect, set "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D\/textureFilter-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D\/TextureFilter-swift.enum\/linearWithMipmapsAnisotropic","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D\/TextureFilter-swift.enum\/nearestWithMipmapsAnisotropic","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" on materials.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In 2D, for this setting to have an effect, set ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CanvasItem\/textureFilter-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CanvasItem\/TextureFilter-swift.enum\/linearWithMipmapsAnisotrop